    "summary": "This study describes a solid acid catalyzed liquid-phase aromatic nitration reaction using concentrated nitric acid in a continuous flow system. The reaction was conducted at 120°C in dichloroethane (DCE) solvent at 1.0 M concentration using a packed-bed reactor with a volume of 7.85 mL and a flow rate of 0.91 mL/min. The flow process achieved 90% yield compared to 92% yield in the corresponding batch reaction conducted under similar conditions (120°C, 1 hour reaction time). The continuous flow approach enabled safe handling of the highly exothermic and potentially hazardous nitration reaction with concentrated nitric acid through better heat management and containment in the packed-bed reactor format. A back-pressure regulator was required to maintain proper reaction conditions and prevent solvent vaporization at the elevated temperature.",
